    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45330" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐτρεπ-ίζω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		fut. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιῶ</span>: pf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐτρέπικα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.316.8
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>):—<i>make ready</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξίφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1651
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἃ χρή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					470
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					1.13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.13
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				4.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Sam.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τείχη</span>
			<i>to restore</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.2.4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν σύριγγα</span>
			<i>lubricates</i> the windpipe, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Cord.</u>
				2
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i>get ready for oneself</i>, or something <i>of
				one's own</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.123
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.619
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be prepared, made ready</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1111
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				626
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς] ἱστίοις -ομένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφαγαῖσιν ηὐτρεπισμένος</span>
			<i>ready for</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				614
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				18.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Mis.</u>
				362b
			</span></i>; <i>to be performed, executed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Po.</u>
				5.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Medic.,
				<i>treat</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Loc.Hom.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, al.; dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				13.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>win over, conciliate</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					4.8.12
				</span></i>
			:—so in 
				Med.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i>: pf.
			
				Pass.
			, in med. sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅπαντας ηὐτρέπισται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.175
				</span></i>
			.</div>
